WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.696
Meet Professor Jason Arday, diagnosed with autism spectrum

00:00:03.696 --> 00:00:07.068
disorder at the age of three. A man who couldn't speak

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:10.746
until the age of 11 and couldn't read or write until he was

00:00:10.746 --> 00:00:12.680
18.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.599
Hello, Jason, As she always did. And I just responded.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.624
Hello. It's quite a strange thing to hear your own voice

00:00:18.624 --> 00:00:21.809
for the first time when you're 11. I didn't expect my voice

00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:24.781
to sound like this. Doctors once believed he might need

00:00:24.781 --> 00:00:27.754
lifelong care, but he chose a different path. He turned

00:00:27.754 --> 00:00:30.885
struggle into strength and a dream into reality. Today, he

00:00:30.885 --> 00:00:33.911
is a professor at the University of Cambridge and one of

00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:36.960
the youngest black professors in its history.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.112
Now he's bringing that powerful story and Global Insight to

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:45.196
the African Allied Health Care Summit 2026 in Accra, Ghana

00:00:45.196 --> 00:00:47.280
as a keynote speaker.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.521
This is more than just the talk, it's a chance to learn

00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:53.994
from a mind that redefined what's possible. If you're ready

00:00:53.994 --> 00:00:57.409
to be inspired, challenged, and transformed, this is where

00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:00.534
you need to be. Register now and be part of something

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.940
bigger.